# Human-owned knobs for the credit CEF discount sleeve.
#
# RUNG LADDER — raise ONE rung at a time, each a deliberate human edit:
#   RUNG-0  DRY_RUN=1  EXECUTION=simulator   compute + log targets only
#   RUNG-1  DRY_RUN=0  EXECUTION=simulator   live shadow ledger, no orders sent
#   RUNG-2  DRY_RUN=0  EXECUTION=ibkr        real orders to the IBKR PAPER account
#
# CURRENT RUNG: RUNG-2, re-armed 2026-07-31 after the halt described below.
#
# HALTED 17:03 ET, RESTORED 18:0x. The sleeve seeded `_live_positions` from the
# shadow ledger, which read flat while the account held $2.07M gross, so the next
# fire would have re-bought the entire $750k book against 164,500 CAD of excess
# liquidity at 83% margin use. Root cause was a missing config/costs.yaml entry
# crashing ops/ledger.py mid-write AFTER orders had transmitted.
#
# Safe to run again because `arm()` now gates every live session: it adopts
# quantities from ib.positions() while keeping the ledger's attribution, consults
# sibling book specs so a symbol another book also trades is never taken from the
# account net, and raises NotArmed rather than transmitting on unverified state.
# Verified 2026-07-31: this book arms clean, phase0 arms clean with all 14
# attributions correct.
#
# NOT IDEMPOTENT: each armed run stacks another order set at the broker, there is
# no dedupe. Cancel pending orders before re-running by hand. The scheduler fires
# once a day, so this only bites manual runs.
#
# ORIGINAL: CURRENT RUNG: RUNG-2. Paper account DUQ199038, no real capital.
# This sleeve cleared the full gate battery on 2026-07-31: PIT universe,
# 9/9 purged walk-forward blocks positive, bootstrap P(SR<=0)=0.000%,
# deflated Sharpe 0.956, Test 7 carry/beta 5/5 factor limits with R2 0.005.
#
# KILL RULE (pre-committed, reviewed at session 60 and not before):
#   (a) live net Sharpe < 0.0, or
#   (b) realised slippage > 2x modelled for 5 consecutive sessions, or
#   (c) top-minus-bottom discount spread < 12% (half its current 22.5%).

